---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
const pageSchema = {
  '@context':'https://schema.org', '@type':'Service', '@id':`${site.url}/estimating-documentation/#service`,
  name:'Professional Estimating & Documentation',
  description:'Professional inspection, technical research, repair planning, and documentation for appropriate vehicle repairs.',
  url:`${site.url}/estimating-documentation/`, provider:{'@id':`${site.url}/#business`}
};
---
<Layout title="Professional Estimating & Documentation | Peak Country" description="Professional vehicle inspection, repair planning, technical research, written estimates, and documentation when a Free Initial Assessment is not enough." exactTitle pageSchema={pageSchema}>
  <header class="page-head estimating-head"><div class="eyebrow">After a conversation, when appropriate</div><h1>Professional Estimating &amp; Documentation</h1><p>Some repairs need more than a quick visual assessment. When formal repair planning, insurance documentation, OEM research, or supporting repair information is needed, Peak Country explains the appropriate professional service first.</p><div class="about-actions"><a class="button" href="/free-hail-inspection/">Start with a Free Initial Assessment →</a><a class="text-link" href={`tel:${site.phone}`}>Call {site.phoneDisplay} →</a></div></header>
  <section class="section estimating-explainer"><div><div class="eyebrow">Professional work, not an estimate store</div><h2>More than someone looking at the vehicle.</h2><p>The fee reflects professional inspection, technical research, repair planning, and documentation required to build a defensible repair plan—not merely the time spent looking at the damage.</p><p>Depending on the vehicle and repair, this may include detailed inspection, PDR lighting, damage analysis, repair planning, OEM research, manufacturer procedures or position statements, R&amp;I research, professional repair-information resources, commercial estimating resources, photographs, supporting technical documentation, written estimate preparation, estimate review, and supplement preparation where appropriate.</p></div><aside><strong>Talk first. Pay only when needed.</strong><ol><li>The appropriate service is identified.</li><li>The service and price are explained.</li><li>You agree before paid work begins.</li></ol><p>No money is collected simply because you click Get Started, submit an inquiry, send photos, ask about insurance, request an inspection, or ask a question.</p></aside></section>
  <section class="section estimating-services"><div class="section-heading"><div class="eyebrow">When more detailed documentation is needed</div><h2>Professional services, explained clearly.</h2><p>These are not subscriptions or online purchases. We determine whether one is useful after the initial conversation.</p></div><div class="estimating-service-list">
    <article><div class="service-price">$99</div><div><h3>Non-Hail PDR Estimate &amp; Documentation</h3><p>For individual dents, creases, body-line damage, and other non-hail PDR repairs when formal documentation is needed. Straightforward customer-pay PDR may still receive a verbal price or range during the Free Initial Assessment.</p></div></article>
    <article><div class="service-price">$149</div><div><h3>Comprehensive Estimate Review</h3><p>For hail or collision repairs where an existing estimate needs detailed professional review.</p><p class="fine"><strong>Typical time:</strong> 60–90 minutes.</p></div></article>
    <article><div class="service-price">$249</div><div><h3>Comprehensive Hail Estimate</h3><p>A complete insurance repair-ready hail evaluation, including detailed panel inspection, specialized PDR lighting, damage documentation, repair planning, OEM research, supporting technical information, and a completed written estimate.</p><p class="fine"><strong>Typical time:</strong> 90–120 minutes.</p></div></article>
  </div></section>
  <section class="section estimate-credit"><div><div class="eyebrow">Estimate-fee credit</div><h2>Applied toward the repair when the documented plan is performed.</h2></div><div><p>If Peak Country performs the repair according to the documented repair plan, the applicable estimating fee is credited in full toward the repair.</p><p>If the final authorized repair scope or repair method changes, the credit may be adjusted to reflect the repair actually performed.</p></div></section>
  <section class="section estimating-links"><div><div class="eyebrow">Keep the next step simple</div><h2>Start with the assessment. We’ll explain if more is needed.</h2><p>A paid professional service begins only after the service and price are explained and you agree. There is no generic website checkout funnel.</p><a class="button" href="/free-hail-inspection/">Get Started →</a></div><nav aria-label="Related estimating resources"><a href="/faq/#insurance-questions">Insurance FAQ →</a><a href="/repair-standards/">Repair Evaluation →</a><a href="/auto-hail-repair/">Hail Repair →</a><a href="/paintless-dent-repair/">PDR →</a><a href="/free-hail-inspection/">Free Initial Assessment →</a></nav></section>
</Layout>
